{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-explainer-about-horse-riding-for-kids-use-very-simple-english-and-the-most-common-words/audio/main-c43a342e0be3.mp3","durationSec":151.224,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.04,"text":"People ride horses for fun, work, and sport."},{"start":3.96,"end":6.06,"text":"Some people enjoy a quiet ride outside."},{"start":7,"end":8.94,"text":"Police officers may ride horses at work."},{"start":9.66,"end":13.48,"text":"In the Olympic Games, riders do sports such as jumping and dressage."},{"start":14.44,"end":17.66,"text":"In dressage, the horse does careful moves when the rider asks."},{"start":18.74,"end":22.76,"text":"Horse riding is teamwork: the rider gives small signs, and the horse answers."},{"start":23.98,"end":26.78,"text":"Horse riding for kids starts slowly at a riding school."},{"start":27.4,"end":31.86,"text":"Charlotte Dujardin also began with a quiet walk, not a race."},{"start":32.96,"end":35.54,"text":"A new rider should start at a good riding school with a teacher."},{"start":36.24,"end":38.54,"text":"The first horse is often quiet and kind."},{"start":39.56,"end":43.56,"text":"The teacher may lead the horse around an arena, which is a safe place for riding."},{"start":44.26,"end":45.84,"text":"The horse usually walks slowly."},{"start":46.58,"end":50.16,"text":"Sometimes the rider tries a short trot, which feels more bouncy."},{"start":50.94,"end":52.18,"text":"There is no need to hurry."},{"start":52.82,"end":56.3,"text":"Always wear a riding helmet that fits well and is closed under your chin."},{"start":56.3,"end":59.04,"text":"A riding helmet helps protect your head if you fall."},{"start":59.94,"end":61.72,"text":"Wear strong boots that cover your ankles."},{"start":62.54,"end":64.62,"text":"Do not walk behind a horse because it may kick."},{"start":65.52,"end":66.88,"text":"Walk to the horse from the side."},{"start":67.5,"end":71.18,"text":"Talk softly and move gently, so the horse knows you are there."},{"start":72.46,"end":74.4,"text":"A saddle is the seat on the horse’s back."},{"start":75.12,"end":77.1,"text":"A strap under the horse holds it in place."},{"start":77.86,"end":80.84,"text":"The saddle spreads the rider’s weight across the horse’s back."},{"start":81.52,"end":83.16,"text":"This helps the horse stay comfortable."},{"start":84,"end":86.24,"text":"Stirrups hang on both sides of the saddle."},{"start":87.02,"end":89.24,"text":"The rider puts a foot in each stirrup for balance."},{"start":90.32,"end":93.32,"text":"Boots with heels help stop the feet from sliding through."},{"start":94.42,"end":98.62,"text":"Reins are long straps that go from the rider’s hands to the horse’s bridle."},{"start":99.34,"end":101.44,"text":"The bridle is the gear on the horse’s head."},{"start":102.52,"end":106.64,"text":"Reins help a rider ask the horse to turn, slow down, or stop."},{"start":107.38,"end":112.2,"text":"They are a little like a steering wheel, but riders must use small, soft moves."},{"start":112.7,"end":114.1,"text":"Pulling hard can hurt the horse."},{"start":114.1,"end":117.06,"text":"Riders also use their legs and body."},{"start":117.06,"end":120.88,"text":"Charlotte Dujardin rode Valegro in dressage."},{"start":121.48,"end":127.5,"text":"They won individual Olympic gold in London in 2012 and Rio in 2016."},{"start":128.92,"end":131.22,"text":"Frankie Dettori was a famous race rider."},{"start":131.72,"end":136.06,"text":"In 1996, he won all seven races on one day at Ascot."},{"start":137.02,"end":143.58,"text":"Ron Turcotte rode the fast racehorse Secretariat, which won the US Triple Crown in 1973."},{"start":143.58,"end":150.74,"text":"Famous riders go fast or do hard moves, but new riders begin with a slow walk."}],"words":[{"text":"People","start":0,"end":0.3},{"text":"ride","start":0.3,"end":0.52},{"text":"horses","start":0.52,"end":0.84},{"text":"for","start":0.84,"end":1.12},{"text":"fun","start":1.12,"end":1.42},{"t